cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "Arbitrarily long runs of consecutive integers with equal Collatz height"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction/tree/main/equal-collatz-heights"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained construction and Lean proof of arbitrarily long runs of
  consecutive positive integers with equal finite Collatz height and equal
  odd-step counts. More generally, every finite pattern of nonnegative
  offsets has arbitrarily large translates with these properties. Height
  is first arrival at one under the shortcut map with odd step (3n+1)/2.
  The result does not prove convergence from an arbitrary prescribed start.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - Collatz height
  - consecutive integers
  - Lean
  - formal verification
